^{:go/end 133} (go/method ReadFromIP "ReadFromIP acts like ReadFrom but returns an IPAddr.\n" [^{:tag (* IPConn)} c ^{:tag (slice byte)} b] :results [int (* IPAddr) error]
  (when (not ^{:go/via [conn]} (.ok c))
    (return 0 nil syscall/EINVAL))

  (let [(values n addr err) (.readFrom c b)]
    (when (!= err nil)
      (set! err (addr (lit OpError :Op "read" :Net (.-net ^{:go/via [conn]} (.-fd c)) :Source (.-laddr ^{:go/via [conn]} (.-fd c)) :Addr (.-raddr ^{:go/via [conn]} (.-fd c)) :Err err))))

    (return n addr err)))



^{:go/end 148} (go/method ReadFrom "ReadFrom implements the [PacketConn] ReadFrom method.\n" [^{:tag (* IPConn)} c ^{:tag (slice byte)} b] :results [int Addr error]
  (when (not ^{:go/via [conn]} (.ok c))
    (return 0 nil syscall/EINVAL))

  (let [(values n addr err) (.readFrom c b)]
    (when (!= err nil)
      (set! err (addr (lit OpError :Op "read" :Net (.-net ^{:go/via [conn]} (.-fd c)) :Source (.-laddr ^{:go/via [conn]} (.-fd c)) :Addr (.-raddr ^{:go/via [conn]} (.-fd c)) :Err err))))

    (when (== addr nil)
      (return n nil err))

    (return n addr err)))









^{:go/end 166} (go/method ReadMsgIP "ReadMsgIP reads a message from c, copying the payload into b and\nthe associated out-of-band data into oob. It returns the number of\nbytes copied into b, the number of bytes copied into oob, the flags\nthat were set on the message and the source address of the message.\n\nThe packages golang.org/x/net/ipv4 and golang.org/x/net/ipv6 can be\nused to manipulate IP-level socket options in oob.\n" [^{:tag (* IPConn)} c ^{:tag (slice byte)} b ^{:tag (slice byte)} oob] :results [^int n ^int oobn ^int flags ^{:tag (* IPAddr)} addr ^error err]
  (when (not ^{:go/via [conn]} (.ok c))
    (return 0 0 0 nil syscall/EINVAL))

  (set! (values n oobn flags addr err) (.readMsg c b oob))
  (when (!= err nil)
    (set! err (addr (lit OpError :Op "read" :Net (.-net ^{:go/via [conn]} (.-fd c)) :Source (.-laddr ^{:go/via [conn]} (.-fd c)) :Addr (.-raddr ^{:go/via [conn]} (.-fd c)) :Err err))))

  (return))



^{:go/end 178} (go/method WriteToIP "WriteToIP acts like [IPConn.WriteTo] but takes an [IPAddr].\n" [^{:tag (* IPConn)} c ^{:tag (slice byte)} b ^{:tag (* IPAddr)} addr] :results [int error]
