^{:go/end 239} (go/func dialIP [^context/Context ctx ^{:tag (* Dialer)} dialer ^string network ^{:tag (* IPAddr)} laddr ^{:tag (* IPAddr)} raddr] :results [(* IPConn) error]
  (when (== raddr nil)
    (return nil (addr (lit OpError :Op "dial" :Net network :Source (.opAddr laddr) :Addr nil :Err errMissingAddress))))

  (let [sd (addr (lit sysDialer :network network :address (.String raddr)))]
    (when (!= dialer nil)
      (set! (.-Dialer sd) @dialer))

    (let [(values c err) (.dialIP sd ctx laddr raddr)]
      (when (!= err nil)
        (return nil (addr (lit OpError :Op "dial" :Net network :Source (.opAddr laddr) :Addr (.opAddr raddr) :Err err))))

      (return c nil))))









^{:go/end 258} (go/func ListenIP "ListenIP acts like [ListenPacket] for IP networks.\n\nThe network must be an IP network name; see func Dial for details.\n\nIf the IP field of laddr is nil or an unspecified IP address,\nListenIP listens on all available IP addresses of the local system\nexcept multicast IP addresses.\n" [^string network ^{:tag (* IPAddr)} laddr] :results [(* IPConn) error]
  (when (== laddr nil)
    (set! laddr (addr (lit IPAddr))))

  (let [sl (addr (lit sysListener :network network :address (.String laddr)))
      (values c err) (.listenIP sl (context/Background) laddr)]
    (when (!= err nil)
      (return nil (addr (lit OpError :Op "listen" :Net network :Source nil :Addr (.opAddr laddr) :Err err))))

    (return c nil)))
